          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "{}\n### Summary of Changes\n\nIn [`dspy/adapters/types/tool.py`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-p3ij5gy_/repo/dspy/adapters/types/tool.py), added flexible input validation and normalization to [`ToolCalls`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-p3ij5gy_/repo/dspy/adapters/types/tool.py#L261) using `@pydantic.model_validator(mode=\"before\")` on `ToolCalls.validate_input`:\n\n1. **Single-object normalization**: If the data is a dictionary containing `name` and `args` (and not already containing `tool_calls`), it wraps the item into `{\"tool_calls\": [data]}`.\n2. **List normalization**: If the data is a list of dictionaries where each item has `name` and `args`, it wraps them into `{\"tool_calls\": data}`.\n3. **Existing behavior preserved**: If `tool_calls` is already present in a dictionary, it is returned as-is. Instances of `ToolCalls` are also returned as-is.\n4. **String handling**: If given a JSON string, it parses the JSON first before normalizing or returning the parsed object; if the string is non-JSON or cannot be parsed, it returns the original string unchanged.\n5. All adapter unit tests passed.\n",
